Test Case ID	
TC-CTBP5001-010	
Test Scenario	
Verify that a record already transmitted but still awaiting the status-message reply is NOT re-extracted
Test Data	
Query 1: List the (report year, receiving country) combinations that are still in transit,already transmitted via CTS and the status message has not been received yet
SELECT RPT_YR, REC_JDX_CTRY
FROM ctsg_enc.V_CTRY_TRANSMISSION;

Query 2: Confirm at the document-reference level that the underlying flag is 'Y'
SELECT DISTINCT REC_JDX_CTRY, TRANSMISSION_FLAG
FROM ctsg_enc.CTS_GSEC_DOC_REF
WHERE TRANSMISSION_FLAG = 'Y';

Query 3: Check that none of the in-transit combinations appear in the extraction driver list
SELECT *
FROM ctsg_enc.V_EXT
WHERE (RPT_YR, REC_JDX_CTRY) IN
      (SELECT RPT_YR, REC_JDX_CTRY FROM ctsg_enc.V_CTRY_TRANSMISSION);

Expected Result
"Query 1 returns at least one (RPT_YR, REC_JDX_CTRY) combination, i.e. records with TRANSMISSION_FLAG = 'Y' are treated as in transit.
Query 2 returns rows with TRANSMISSION_FLAG = 'Y', matching the combinations in Query 1.
Query 3 returns no rows, i.e. records transmitted but still awaiting the status message are not re-extracted."
